#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Definition]
#title[Rectangle]

The authors in #local("00GF")[arXiv:math/0503436v2] define a square on a finite set $S$ to be a pair of equivalence relations $(R_1, R_2)$ such that every equivalence class of $R_1$ intersect every equivalance class of $R_2$ in exactly one element.

$
  "Rectangle"(S) :-= sum_(R_1,R_2 : "Eq-Rel"(S)) product_(x,y : S) "is-contr"(sum_(z:S) R_1 (x,z) xx R_2 (y,z) )
$

This structure was first introduced in #local("00GG")[arXiv:math/0210057v2] under the term _cartesian decomposition_.
